nsity of vastus muscle activity during functional activities in subjects with and without patellofemoral pain</article-title><source>Physical Therapy</source><year>1996</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>946</fpage><lpage>955</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8790273</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sheehy</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Burdett</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name><name><surname>Irrgang</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>VanSwearingen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An electromyographic study of vastus medialis oblique and vastus lateralis activity while ascending and descending steps</article-title><source>J Orthop Sports Phys Ther</source><year>1998</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>423</fpage><lpage>429</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9617728</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cowan</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bennell</surname><given-names>KL</given-names></name><name><surname>Hodges</surname><given-names>PW</given-names></name><name><surname>Crossley</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>McConnell</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Delayed onset of electromyographic activity of vastus medialis obliquus relative to vastus lateralis in subjects with patellofemoral pain syndrome</article-title><source>Archives of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation</source><year>2001</year><volume>82</volume><fpage>183</fpage><lpage>189</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11239308</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1053/apmr.2001.19022</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dixon</surname><given-name