 osteoarthritis</article-title><source>Archives of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation</source><year>2005</year><volume>86</volume><fpage>871</fpage><lpage>875</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15895330</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.apmr.2004.09.018</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>American Podiatric Medical Association. High Heel Survey 2003</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.apma.org/s_apma/doc.asp?CID=385&#x00026;DID=17112"/><comment>Accessed 23 November 2006</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hertel</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Sloss</surname><given-names>BR</given-names></name><name><surname>Earl</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of foot orthotics on quadriceps and gluteus medius electromyographic activity during selected exercises</article-title><source>Archives of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation</source><year>2005</year><volume>86</volume><fpage>26</fpage><lpage>30</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15640985</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.apmr.2004.03.029</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stefanyshyn</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Nigg</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><name><surname>Fisher</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Flynn</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The influence of high heeled shoes on kinematics, kinetics, and muscle EMG of normal female gait</article-title><source>Journal of Applied Biomechanics</source><year>2000</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>309</fpage><lpage>319</lpage></citation></ref><ref i